### Ordering API — manual requests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client)
# Standalone the service listens on 8080. Under `aspire run` the host port is
# dynamic: copy the ordering endpoint from the Aspire dashboard into @baseUrl.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Root — 200 text/plain "Ordering API is running."
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Health — 200 {"status":"UP"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Create order — 201, total 39.30, 2 items, no Location header
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "buyerId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "items": [
    { "productId": 1, "productName": "Mug", "unitPrice": 9.90, "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": 2, "productName": "Tee", "unitPrice": 19.50, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Invalid: empty items — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "buyerId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111", "items": [] }

### Invalid: quantity 0 — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "buyerId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "items": [{ "productId": 1, "productName": "Mug", "unitPrice": 9.90, "quantity": 0 }]
}

### Invalid: negative price — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "buyerId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "items": [{ "productId": 1, "productName": "Mug", "unitPrice": -0.01, "quantity": 1 }]
}

### Invalid: price with three decimals — 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "buyerId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "items": [{ "productId": 1, "productName": "Mug", "unitPrice": 9.999, "quantity": 1 }]
}
